<article class="env-definition" id="5033D5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/5033D5">Definition <span data-tag="5033D5">6.1.4.1</span>.</a>left exact!at an object $Z$ Let $f: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a functor between $\infty $-categories which admit finite limits. Let $Z$ be an object of $\calX $. We will say that $f$ is <em>left exact at $Z$</em> if, for every pullback square </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { W \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  Y \ar [d] \\ X \ar [r] &amp;  Z } \]
</div>
  <p> in $\calX $, the induced square </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { f(W) \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  f(Y) \ar [d] \\ f(X) \ar [r] &amp;  f(Z) } \]
</div>
  <p> is a pullback in $\calY $. </p>
</article>